<main class="faq">
  <h1>AI Consulting in Nigeria</h1>
  <p class="lead">We are an AI consulting and engineering firm registered in Nigeria, with our office in Oniru, Victoria Island, Lagos. We help Nigerian banks, government bodies and businesses decide where AI can genuinely help, train their people to use it well, and build tools that hold up in daily work.</p>
  <section><h2>Why Nigerian organisations work with us</h2><p>Plenty of firms can talk about AI. The harder part is making it work here: with Nigerian data rules, Nigerian infrastructure, and teams that need to run the system long after the consultants leave. That is the work we do. We are registered with the Corporate Affairs Commission, founded in 2024 by Supreme Oyewumi and Kola Olatunde, and we build for Nigerian reality first.</p><p>Our early work includes AI training delivered in partnership with a state government, workforce programmes for enterprise and public-sector teams, and agent and automation builds for businesses that needed real results, not demonstrations.</p></section><section><h2>What we do</h2><p>Three things, kept simple. First, <a href='/our-services/ai-strategy-advisory/'>strategy</a>: we help your leadership decide where AI is worth the money, what to do first and who should own it. Second, <a href='/our-services/ai-training-workforce-development/'>training</a>: practical programmes that take executives, managers and staff from curious to capable. Third, <a href='/our-services/ai-agent-automation-engineering/'>building</a>: AI agents and automation that take over repetitive work in operations, support and finance, with your people staying in control.</p><p>We also build our own products, including <a href='https://migratio.cognis.group'>Migratio</a>, a data migration platform designed for banks and regulated Nigerian institutions.</p></section><section><h2>Data rules are not an afterthought</h2><p>Nigerian organisations answer to the NDPA 2023, and banks answer to CBN guidance on top of it. We treat those rules as design inputs: where your data must stay in-country, we design for that from the start. Read more about our approach on the <a href='/ndpa-compliant-ai/'>NDPA-compliant AI</a> page.</p></section>
  <section>
    <h2>Common questions</h2>
    <details><summary>Do you work outside Lagos?</summary><p>Yes. We are based in Lagos and work with organisations across Nigeria, on site and remotely. Much of our training and advisory work happens inside client offices.</p></details><details><summary>How much does AI consulting cost in Nigeria?</summary><p>It depends on scope. Strategy engagements are fixed-fee, and build work is priced in phases with milestone-based release. The first conversation is free and confidential, and we tell you honestly whether we are the right firm for the problem.</p></details><details><summary>Can you train a team that has never used AI?</summary><p>Yes, that is the most common starting point. Our programmes are role-based, from executive sessions to hands-on staff training, and are anchored to your organisation’s actual work rather than generic examples.</p></details><details><summary>How do we start?</summary><p>Write to <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection" class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="0e676068614e6d616960677d20697c617b7e">[email&#160;protected]</a> or use the contact form. A senior team member replies within two business days.</p></details>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Talk to us</h2>
    <p>The first conversation is free, confidential and honest: our job in that call is to understand the problem well enough to tell you whether we are the right firm for it. Write to <a href="/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#9cf5f2faf3dcfff3fbf2f5efb2fbeef3e9ec"><span class="__cf_email__" data-cfemail="422b2c242d02212d252c2b316c25302d3732">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> or use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a>.</p>
  </section>
</main>

